# Wurmwall Sweeper: "4+ | Flying" with its 2/2 box (CR 721.2b: "as long as this permanent has N or more charge counters on it,
# it has [abilities] and is a creature with base power and toughness [P/T] in addition to its other types"). It enters, surveils
# 2 (the Island to the graveyard, Vampire Hexmage kept on top), and is an artifact with no power or toughness (CR 721.2c, 208.3).
# Sunset Saboteur (4 power, cast this turn) stations it to exactly four counters: it is a 2/2 flying artifact creature, and
# summoning sick, having come under Bot1's control this turn (CR 302.6). On turn 3 it may attack: what matters is how long it
# has been on the battlefield, not how long it has been a creature (ruling 2025-07-25). Station taps "another" creature: the
# Sweeper, an untapped creature now, can't pay its own station cost. Then Vampire Hexmage removes all its counters: below
# four it is no creature and has no flying (ruling: "if a permanent with station ... loses charge counters somehow, its
# abilities change accordingly. The same is true for determining whether or not that permanent is a creature").

